# SAFAR Project Rules & System Brief (SIH Problem Statement 26265)
# Team: Code Blooded | AICTE Regulation Bureau | Smart Automation

## 1. Project Overview & Identity
- **Product Name:** SAFAR — Smart AICTE FDR Automation & Registry
- **Objective:** Streamline the lifecycle of Fixed Deposit Receipts (FDR) and Bank Guarantees (BG) submitted by technical institutions to AICTE as security deposits.
- **Key Principle:** Keep what an institution SUBMITS strictly separate from what an issuing bank INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMS. Never advance or release an instrument on the institution's word alone.
- **Simulation Disclaimer:** All bank verification calls and confirmation responses are SIMULATED in this prototype using mock adapters. Never claim real core banking API connections. Label all simulated components clearly in UI, code, and docs.

---

## 2. Architecture & Layout Conventions
This project follows a **FLAT BACKEND LAYOUT** and **REACT + VITE FRONTEND**:

```text
SAFAR-SIH26265/
